Friday Update
* Trade Alert: Buy MCD calls; Adjust target for CCL calls*&nbsp;Stocks jump=
 around the unchanged line following weak jobs report.Stocks were swirling =
in all directions Friday as COVID-19 stimulus checks were distributed and j=
ob indicators showed that while payrolls unexpectedly declined, there were =
other positive signs for Wall Street.Nonfarm payrolls in the December emplo=
yment report fell by 140,000, worse than the increase of 50,000 that was th=
e consensus on Econday. The unemployment rate stayed at 6.7% in December, b=
elow the 6.8% rate expected."On an annualized basis, 8% more hours were wor=
ked in the fourth quarter than in the third quarter. This suggests a signif=
icant increase in (gross domestic product) in the final quarter of 2020," C=
hristoph Balz, senior economist at Commerzbank, said in a report. "The sign=
s are also good that the U.S. economy will continue to recover. Short-term =
indicators of the labor market, such as weekly initial jobless claims, have=
 stabilized."The report came as the $600 checks in approved pandemic stimul=
us checks have begun to be distributed to Americans. The chance that relief=
 could rise more than threefold looked increasingly possible following the =
win of Democratic candidates in the Georgia Senate runoff vote this week.On=
 the Dow Jones Industrial Average, Salesforce.com (CRM) and Chevron (CVX) w=
ere both rising nearly 1.6% in the biggest gains as the 30 blue-chip compon=
ents were about split between advancers and declines. 3M (MMM) had the stee=
pest decrease, with a 1.7% drop. The measure gave back its early gains and =
slipped into the red within the first hour of trading.In company news New R=
elic (NEWR) rose 16% after it said it expects its fiscal 2021 results above=
 the high end of its guidance. Sarepta Therapeutics (SRPT) fell 50% after s=
aying late Thursday its experimental drug SRP-9001 trial met the primary bi=
ological endpoint in a trial at 12 weeks but did not show statistical signi=
ficance on a primary functional endpoint. Several analysts including RBC an=
d Goldman Sachs cut their price targets on the shares.Portfolio: Our order =
for CCL calls filled. The price action is squirrelly so adjust target/stop.=
 Order for TSM calls did not fill. We have one new idea for you.*CURRENT RE=
COMMENDATION&nbsp;Carnival Corp. (CCL) January 15 calls-- Symbol: CCL210115=
C00015000-- Bought Jan 7 at $5.80.&nbsp;-- Now trading at $5.60.-- Set up t=
o sell ALL of the calls at new $5.85 lmt gtc-- Set stop at new $5.00, good =
anytime.&nbsp;*NEW RECOMMENDATIONMcDonald=E2=80=99s Corp. (MCD) February 22=
0 calls-- Symbol: MCD210219C00220000-- Order: Buy at $4.30 lmt day only-- I=
f filled, set up to sell half at $5.60 lmt gtc and half at $7.30 lmt gtc-- =
If filled, set stop at $3.00 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Jon D. Mark=
manAll recommendations are for monthly options expiring on the third Friday=
 of the specified month unless otherwise noted. All stops are good after 10=
:30 a.m. Eastern only unless otherwise specified. All orders are good for t=
he day only unless otherwise noted. "Day only" orders expire at the close o=
